config MLX90395
	bool "MLX90395 3-axis magnetometer"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_MELEXIS_MLX90395_ENABLED
	select I2C
	select CRC
	help
	  Enable driver for the Melexis MLX90395 3-axis magnetometer, in
	  both its 50 mT and 120 mT variants.

config MLX90395_PIPELINED
	bool "Do not wait for the conversion in sample_fetch"
	depends on MLX90395
	help
	  By default a fetch starts a single measurement and sleeps until
	  it is done, which takes up to ~105 ms with the oversampling and
	  digital filter at their maximum.

	  With this option a fetch instead collects the measurement the
	  previous fetch started, starts the next one and returns at once.
	  A fetch made before that conversion is done returns -EBUSY, and
	  so does the very first fetch. Each sample is therefore as old as
	  the interval between fetches, which must be at least the
	  conversion time for every fetch to deliver one.

	  For callers that share a thread with other time-critical work. A
	  plain fetch-then-get, e.g. the sensor shell, sees -EBUSY or a
	  stale sample instead.
